curities, mergers and acquisitions, and financial advisory services. Nomura Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 1925 and is headquartered in Tokyo, Japan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kentaro  Okuda | President, Group CEO, Representative Executive Officer & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $10.4M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 28K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Nomura Holdings Inc is a large-cap financial services business with a $24.9B market cap on $31.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 10% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The company is burning through $8.0B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.11917989207935227},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 37% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Nomura: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nomura-3-key-takeaways-long-220502654.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795212302.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's How Much $100 Invested In Nomura Holdings 5 Years Ago Would Be Worth Today","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/63476626/here-s-how-much-100-invested-nomura-holdings-5-years-ago-would-be-worth-today","dat